const PROCESS_HTML=infoPage('How projects work','TaskForge AI quotation, delivery and payment process for small digital services.','/how-it-works','<section><h2>1. Share a redacted scope</h2><p>Describe the deliverable, approximate file and row counts, systems involved, time constraints and acceptance checks using the free inquiry form. Do not send private credentials or unrestricted records.</p><h2>2. Feasibility and quote</h2><p>We review whether the work can be delivered safely. If feasible, scope, price, currency and schedule are explicitly agreed before payment. Some requests are not supported. No prices on this site should be inferred from demonstration data.</p><h2>3. Approved payment and work</h2><p>A payment or escrow method is confirmed individually for each approved order. Do not pay based on a test checkout or an unsolicited link. Work proceeds only against an agreed, funded scope.</p><h2>4. Delivery and quality check</h2><p>We validate the deliverable against agreed rules and identify exceptions rather than invent missing information. Changes outside scope require separate review. Browser demonstrations use fictional data and do not imply past paid engagements.</p><p><a style="color:#9fe6b8" href="/contact#tf-scope">Request a scoped quote</a></p></section>');
const PRIVACY_HTML=infoPage('Privacy and data handling','Privacy information for TaskForge AI website inquiries, example demos and project requests.','/privacy','<p><strong>What an inquiry collects:</strong> name, email, optional company, your project description and a budget range. These details are sent to our hosted Supabase intake database to review your request. Do not send credentials or unredacted customer records in the inquiry form.</p><p><strong>Optional project uploads:</strong> the separate project-submission workflow may accept a document for scope review. Only upload files you are authorized to share. No charge is taken just for submitting.</p><p><strong>Website measurement:</strong> selected marketing pages use Cloudflare Web Analytics to assess performance. The fictional-data browser demos do not transmit their input fields to TaskForge.</p><p><strong>Payment:</strong> individual approved checkout processes may use an external payment service; do not assume a payment has succeeded until the transaction is confirmed. We do not ask for card numbers in inquiry forms.</p><p><strong>Data correction or deletion:</strong> use the <a href="/contact#tf-scope" style="color:#9fe6b8">contact form</a> and specify your request. We will assess it based on the data available and applicable requirements. This page does not promise a fixed retention period.</p><p>Current published information describes the live website functions; it is not a substitute for signed project terms or the privacy policies of third-party providers.</p>');
const EXAMPLES_HTML=infoPage('Demonstrations and capabilities','Fictional-data TaskForge AI demonstrations and operational scopes, not client case studies.','/examples','<p>Every demonstration here uses fictional or synthetic data. These are not testimonials, paid client engagements, testimonials or verified client outcomes.</p><section><h2>Browser demos you can inspect</h2><ul><li><a href="/automation/leadops" style="color:#9fe6b8">LeadOps CSV routing:</a> inspect deduplication flags, deterministic routing and CSV export locally in your browser.</li><li><a href="/automation/crm-cleanup" style="color:#9fe6b8">CRM contact cleanup:</a> review simulated contact comparisons and conflict handling without merging records automatically.</li><li><a href="/automation/inventory-reservations" style="color:#9fe6b8">Distributor inventory reservations:</a> test protected stock commitments, split sources and shortage exceptions.</li></ul><h2 id="consolidation">Fictional spreadsheet consolidation example</h2><p>A controlled three-workbook, 12-row illustration with three flagged records demonstrates source tracing, header mapping and exception review. This page is not a downloadable client workbook; sample review can be arranged when an assessment is scoped.</p><h2 id="restaurant">Fictional restaurant stock workbook</h2><p>A formula-driven illustration covers purchases, stock issues, on-hand quantities, reorder alerts and supplier balance. This is not a live POS deployment, accounting assurance or a previous customer result.</p><p>No integrations, payment or live inventory update can be inferred from these demonstrations.</p><p><a href="/contact#tf-scope" style="color:#9fe6b8">Request a review of a specific deliverable</a></p></section>');
